{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t/**\n2\t * Format-drift re-normalization: the supersession half of the drift story\n3\t * (the preservation half — emitting raw-only `unrecognized` events — lives in\n4\t * adapters/drift.ts). When a newer cledger version has learned to interpret a\n5\t * transcript line type it once preserved raw-only, `renormalize` turns each\n6\t * such stored line into the proper `conversation_turn` and appends a\n7\t * `supersession` event linking the two, so consumers stop seeing the raw\n8\t * placeholder and see the interpreted turn instead.\n9\t *\n10\t * Invariants:\n11\t *  - Append-only. The `unrecognized` event is never deleted; it is superseded\n12\t *    via a `supersession` event carrying `links:[{rel:\"supersedes\",target}]`.\n13\t *  - Idempotent. A second run is a no-op: already-superseded events are\n14\t *    skipped, and every id we produce is deterministic, so `appendEvents`\n15\t *    dedups anything that slips through.\n16\t *  - Id fidelity. The turn is reconstructed by re-feeding the stored `raw.data`\n17\t *    through the owning adapter's *same* convert path (see each adapter's\n18\t *    `renormalizeUnrecognized`), so it gets the exact id a live capture of the\n19\t *    same line would — a future live capture then dedups against it rather\n20\t *    than duplicating.\n21\t *  - Redaction safety. The stored `raw.data` was already redacted at\n22\t *    preservation time; the reconstructed turn also rides the normal\n23\t *    `appendEvents` redaction path, which is idempotent on already-placeholdered\n24\t *    text — nothing is re-exposed.\n25\t *\n26\t * Manual-only for now: this is an explicit `cledger renormalize` step, not\n27\t * auto-triggered on capture. Auto-detecting \"the adapter changed\" and running\n28\t * this after a version bump is a deferred follow-up (see the roadmap).\n29\t */\n30\timport type { RepoInfo } from \"./git.