{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01PZ4E6HDtQyGtUnSxMnZ1k7","input":{"command":"gh pr create --draft --title \"0.20.0: Gemini CLI and Qwen Code adapters\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdds capture for the two CLIs at the top of the README's TODO adapter list, plus a shared conversion core, and fixes a data-loss bug the existing adapters share.\n\nBoth CLIs were installed and driven against a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint to produce real sessions; every format claim below is from a live transcript or from the CLI's own shipped source, not inferred.\n\n## Gemini CLI\n\n`~/.gemini/tmp/<project>/chats/session-*.jsonl`, hooked on `AfterAgent` + `SessionEnd`.\n\nThe file is append-only but is **not** a transcript — it is a write-ahead log of mutations to one conversation document: `$rewindTo` removals, `$set` metadata patches, whole-document `$set.messages` snapshots, and message upserts keyed by a durable id. Capture replays it with Gemini's own record precedence.\n\n**It deliberately does not honour the removals.** On a real session, Gemini rewrote the document with a snapshot that silently dropped the prompt the user had just typed (after a failed API call), so a faithful replay records no trace of it having been asked. The ledger records evidence, so it keeps the union of every message the file ever held, each at its last-written value, and treats removals as facts about Gemini's live view rather than instructions to forget.\n\nThat choice pays off twice: because nothing is removed, `seq` is assigned at first sighting and never reused, so a rewind cannot renumber later turns — the positional-`seq` churn the opencode adapter documents and accepts does not arise here.\n\nA model turn whose tool calls have not settled is withheld and holds the cursor back. Gemini's harness-authored `<session_context>`/`<hook_context>` preambles are captured but attributed to `system`, not to you.\n\n## Qwen Code\n\n`~/.qwen/projects/<escaped-cwd>/chats/<session-id>.jsonl`, hooked on `Stop` + `SessionEnd`.\n\nA fork of Gemini CLI that did *not* inherit its conversation store: plain append-only JSONL with a claude-code-shaped envelope, so this adapter is the claude-code adapter's twin — per-line conversion, line-index `seq`, line-count cursor.\n\nBoth CLIs express content as Google GenAI `Part` lists, so that conversion lives once in `adapters/genai-parts.ts`: a `thought` part becomes a visible `thinking` block, `functionCall`/`functionResponse` become `tool_use`/`tool_result`, and anything unrecognized passes through verbatim inside the turn.\n\n`provider` is left unset on purpose — Qwen records only an *auth mode* (`openai`, `qwen-oauth`), which is not the inference provider the schema asks for.\n\n## Bug fix: torn trailing lines were dropped\n\nThe claude-code and codex adapters advanced the cursor to `lines.length` even when the last line was half-written, so the completed line was never captured — a silent, permanent loss of exactly one turn whenever a hook fired mid-write. All three line-based adapters now hold the cursor at the first unparseable line. Covered by a new test.\n\n## Refactors\n\n- `adapters/common.ts` — `packageVersion`/`sanitizeId`/cursor read+write, previously copy-pasted into all three adapters. Cursor field names are preserved per adapter so no existing cursor on disk resets.\n- `installJsonHooks` — one parameterized writer for the Claude-Code-shaped `settings.json` hook config. Not a coincidence worth duplicating: Gemini ships a `gemini hooks migrate` command to import Claude Code's config, and Qwen forked Gemini's engine. Only the path and event names differ.\n\n## One ugly-but-necessary detail\n\n`install` appends `>/dev/null 2>&1` to the generated hook command for these two CLIs only. Verified on Qwen Code 0.21.5: `qwen -p \"...\"` fires its `Stop` hook and exits immediately, killing the hook process along with the stdio pipes it inherited. A hook that returns instantly survives; a git-notes append does not, and nothing gets captured. A deliberately slow probe hook reproduced it every time. The redirection fixes it reliably (3/3 runs), at the cost of the capture no longer printing drift warnings where you can see them — the same trade the opencode plugin already makes. Documented in the Roadmap; the real fix belongs upstream.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 189 tests, 188 pass / 1 pre-existing skip. 16 new (6 qwen, 10 gemini).\n- End to end: `cledger install qwen-code` → a real `qwen` run editing a file → 6 events captured automatically, reasoning and tool calls included, idempotent on rescan.\n- The real Gemini session captured both messages, including the one faithful replay would have lost, with correct `system` vs `human` attribution.\n\n## Heads-up on overlap\n\nPR #4 (`worktree-capture-everything`, draft) touches the same three existing adapters plus `drift.ts`/`schema.ts`/`renormalize.ts` and claims 0.19.0. This branch takes 0.20.0 and is based on `origin/main`, so whichever merges second will need a rebase — most of the conflict will be in the adapter skip-lists, which that PR removes and this one adds two more of.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open draft PR","timeout":180000},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"289aa52f3a864db2d2404ec55b4b5dc5a987b70b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","seq":796},"id":"ev1-592d5f05ee46ad632bf7cbcc36d9d74347c576b3cf39695a7aca0ff01cf7db4a","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T04:50:56.971Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2