detail\n\n`install` appends `>/dev/null 2>&1` to the generated hook command for these two CLIs only. Verified on Qwen Code 0.21.5: `qwen -p \"...\"` fires its `Stop` hook and exits immediately, killing the hook process along with the stdio pipes it inherited. A hook that returns instantly survives; a git-notes append does not, and nothing gets captured. A deliberately slow probe hook reproduced it every time. The redirection fixes it reliably (3/3 runs), at the cost of the capture no longer printing drift warnings where you can see them — the same trade the opencode plugin already makes. Documented in the Roadmap; the real fix belongs upstream.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 189 tests, 188 pass / 1 pre-existing skip. 16 new (6 qwen, 10 gemini).\n- End to end: `cledger install qwen-code` → a real `qwen` run editing a file → 6 events captured automatically, reasoning and tool calls included, idempotent on rescan.\n- The real Gemini session captured both messages, including the one faithful replay would have lost, with correct `system` vs `human` attribution.\n\n## Heads-up on overlap\n\nPR #4 (`worktree-capture-everything`, draft) touches the same three existing adapters plus `drift.ts`/`schema.ts`/`renormalize.ts` and claims 0.19.0. This branch takes 0.20.0 and is based on `origin/main`, so whichever merges second will need a rebase — most of the conflict will be in the adapter skip-lists, which that PR removes and this one adds two more of.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Ewo7xu7kzLpH4MeEDK5LDc\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open draft PR","timeout":180000},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011Cdh783hT3LmTHKA8G3xJQ","model":"claude-opus-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":401,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":401,"cac