{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01RgTce8jXdadmWNxiq4cusA","input":{"content":"---\nname: project-cledger-gemini-qwen-adapters\ndescription: gemini-cli + qwen-code adapters shipped 0.20.0 (PR #5, draft); gemini WAL union-capture decision, qwen headless hook kill, torn-line cursor fix\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nAdapters for Gemini CLI and Qwen Code, 0.20.0, PR #5 (draft, branch\n`worktree-more-cli-adapters`). Both CLIs were npm-installed globally and driven\nagainst the local ds4-gateway (`http://127.0.0.1:9002/v1`, OpenAI-compatible,\nmodel `deepseek-v4-flash`) to produce real sessions — that endpoint is the cheap\nway to generate real transcripts for any OpenAI-compatible CLI without accounts.\nGemini CLI does *not* accept an OpenAI base URL; its format was pinned from its\nshipped (unminified) bundle at `/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@google/gemini-cli/bundle/`.\n\nDecisions worth remembering:\n\n- **Gemini's session file is a write-ahead log, not a transcript.** Records:\n  `$rewindTo` removal, bare message upsert by durable id, `$set` metadata patch\n  (a `$set.messages` array replaces the whole document), and the\n  `sessionId`+`projectHash` header. Verified: after a failed API call Gemini\n  wrote a snapshot that dropped the prompt the user had just typed. So capture\n  takes the **union** of every message ever written (last value wins) rather\n  than replaying removals — deletions are recorded in `GeminiSession.rewound`\n  instead. Side benefit: `seq` assigned at first sighting is never reused, so\n  rewinds can't renumber later turns (better than opencode's positional seq).\n- **Qwen headless mode kills hooks.** `qwen -p` fires `Stop` then exits,\n  tearing down the hook process. Instant hooks survive; a git-notes append does\n  not. Fix: `install` appends `>/dev/null 2>&1` to the command, which reliably\n  works but costs visible drift warnings. Same trade the opencode plugin makes.\n  Upstream fix would be to await the hook.\n- **Torn trailing line bug (pre-existing, fixed here).** claude-code and codex\n  advanced the cursor to `lines.length` even when the last line was half\n  written, permanently losing that turn. All line-based adapters now hold the\n  cursor at the first unparseable line.\n- Gemini `info`/`error`/`warning` UI notices are skipped, and a rewind is not\n  itself recorded as an event — both left as Roadmap items because they are\n  schema questions, not adapter ones.\n\nOverlaps [[project-cledger-full-capture]] (PR #4, 0.19.0) in the three existing\nadapters; whichever merges second needs a rebase. See also\n[[project-cledger-opencode-adapter]] for the adapter conventions both follow.\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-gemini-qwen-adapters.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"289aa52f3a864db2d2404ec55b4b5dc5a987b70b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","seq":803},"id":"ev1-b604d0659c4e9d1211b8f96ef8225a8d5272e2ea4172a82db55e0bfef61adc8e","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T04:51:28.571Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"8f1a9339-b2b4-4bad-b2a9-3123e47d2a77","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.221","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01RgTce8jXdadmWNxiq4cusA","input":{"content":"---\nname: project-cledger-gemini-qwen-adapters\ndescriptio